    "content": [
      {
        "id": "institutional-introduction",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "An institution visible through scientific exchange",
        "content": "The Institute for Research in Fundamental Sciences appears under the abbreviation IPM in records published by the Abdus Salam International Centre for Theoretical Physics, or ICTP, in Trieste, Italy. These records locate IPM in Tehran and document specific connections in mathematics and physics. They provide evidence of scholarly activity rather than a complete institutional profile. [s1][s2]\n\nThis distinction matters when reading about a research institute. A conference announcement can establish an organizing relationship, while a seminar notice can establish the affiliation reported for a speaker. Neither document, on its own, identifies the institute's complete remit, budget, governing arrangements, or current leadership. Those aspects remain outside the verified scope of this draft. [s1][s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "mathematical-collaboration",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A documented mathematical collaboration",
        "content": "An official ICTP announcement identifies IPM as a co-organizer of a workshop and conference in combinatorics and graph theory scheduled in Trieste for 3–14 September 2012. The program combined advanced teaching with opportunities to discuss current research. Its stated subjects included graph theory, combinatorial designs, algebraic combinatorics, and probabilistic methods. [s1]\n\nThe announcement also names researchers with IPM affiliations in its organizing team. This is a concrete example of institutional participation in international mathematical exchange. As an advance announcement, however, it establishes what was planned; it does not independently prove attendance, completion of every session, or subsequent research outcomes. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "physics-connections",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Physics and cosmology connections",
        "content": "An ICTP seminar notice issued in October 2023 identifies Moslem Ahmadvand with IPM's School of Particles and Accelerators. It announces a talk on a heavy QCD axion model in relation to pulsar timing arrays. The notice supports a narrowly defined conclusion: a researcher was presented with that institutional affiliation for a specialized physics seminar. It does not establish an institute-wide research priority or validate the model discussed. [s2]\n\nEarlier ICTP timetable records also list IPM-affiliated speakers at an advanced school on cosmology in May 2015. The listed subjects include early-universe theory and modified gravity. Together, these documents show how an institutional profile can be built from identifiable scientific activities without substituting reputation claims or rankings for evidence. They should not be read as a census of IPM's researchers or disciplines. [s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "profile-limits",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "What remains to be established",
        "content": "The available records offer a useful entry point into IPM's mathematical and physical-science connections. A publication-ready institutional account still needs accessible primary documentation for its founding, changes of name, governance, current schools, facilities, and educational responsibilities. The main institutional website returned no readable page content during this research, so those details have not been inferred from secondary listings.",
        "source_ids": []
      }
